      "content": "the manual is super vague about it, just says \"posture optimization technology\" which is such a typical corporate way to hide things. i'm really struggling to focus because i feel like i have to control my breathing and my movements just so nothing \"suspicious\" shows up in their metrics. besides just not using it, are there any actual ways to mask my physical signals? like, is there a way to sit so i'm not giving off as much biometric info or something? something that would make the data look \"stable\" or just harder to read?",
